---
/**
 * CareerAgent's behaviour from its README, drawn as a short chat: cited
 * answers, a refusal when the documents cannot support an answer, and
 * per-request cost logging. Synthetic candidate, no real data.
 */
---

<div class="vignette career" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="career-tools">
    <span>search_cv()</span>
    <span>web_research()</span>
  </div>
  <p class="bubble is-user" style="--d:0">Which projects used pgvector?</p>
  <p class="bubble is-agent" style="--d:1">
    Two of them, both in the CV.
    <span class="cite">p.2</span>
    <span class="cite">p.3</span>
  </p>
  <p class="bubble is-user" style="--d:2">What was the team size there?</p>
  <p class="bubble is-agent is-refusal" style="--d:3">
    Not in your documents, so no answer.<span class="caret"></span>
  </p>
  <div class="career-meter">
    <span class="meter-dot"></span>
    tokens and cost logged per request
  </div>
</div>
